{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["If a man causes a field or vineyard to be grazed — he lets his animal feed in another's field." "The best of his field, etc. — from the choicest of his property he pays him, whether land or the monetary equivalent; this is how our Rabbis explained it. And according to the plain sense it implies: according to the best of the field and vineyard of this injured party he pays, for perhaps the animal ate from the choicest part."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:31.712888853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}